      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the equation of the hyperbola that satisfies the given condition \\( |PF_1 - PF_2| = 1 \\). This is known as the definition of a hyperbola where the difference in distances from any point \\(P\\) to two fixed points (called the foci) is constant.\n\nGiven:\n- \\( F_1 = \\left( -3, 1 - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\right) \\)\n- \\( F_2 = \\left( -3, 1 + \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\right) \\)\n- The constant distance difference is \\( |PF_1 - PF_2| = 1 \\).\n\nFirst, we observe that the points \\( F_1 \\) and \\( F_2 \\) are vertically aligned, and the distance between them is:\n\\[\n\\Delta F_1 F_2 = \\left| \\left( 1 + \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\right) - \\left( 1 - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\right) \\right| = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\n\\]\n\nLet \\( h = -3 \\) (the x-coordinate of both foci). Now, we calculate the y-coordinate of the midpoint of the foci \\( M \\):\n\\[\nM = \\left( -3, \\frac{\\left( 1 + \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\right) + \\left( 1 - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\right)}{2} \\right) = \\left( -3, 1 \\right)\n\\]\nThus, the midpoint of \\( F_1 \\) and \\( F_2 \\) is the center of the hyperbola, which is \\( C = \\left( -3, 1 \\right) \\).\n\nThe distance between the foci is \\(\\Delta F_1 F_2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\). For a hyperbola, the distance between the foci is \\( 2c \\), where \\( c \\) is given by:\n\\[\nc = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\n\\]\n\nThe constant difference in distances is 1, so \\( 2a = 1 \\), giving \\( a = \\frac{1}{2} \\).\n\nIn a standard form of a hyperbola:\n\\[\n\\frac{(y - k)^2}{a^2} - \\frac{(x - h)^2}{b^2} = 1\n\\]\n\nSince the y-coordinate of \\( C \\) is 1, \\( k = 1 \\). We can now substitute \\( h \\) and \\( a \\) into the equation:\n\\[\n\\frac{(y - 1)^2}{a^2} - \\frac{(x + 3)^2}{b^2} = 1\n\\]\n\nWe don't know \\( b \\) yet, but we will determine it using the relationship \\( c^2 = a^2 + b^2 \\):\n\\[\nc^2 = \\left( \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\right)^2 = \\frac{5}{4}\n\\]\n\\[\na^2 = \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{4}\n\\]\nTherefore:\n\\[\nb^2 = c^2 - a^2 = \\frac{5}{4} - \\frac{1}{4} = 1\n\\]\n\nThus, \\( b = 1 \\).\n\nFinally, we calculate \\( h + k + a + b \\):\n\\[\nh + k + a + b = -3 + 1 + \\frac{1}{2} + 1 = -0 + \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\nSo, \\( h + k + a + b = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}} \\).",
