      "text": "2016 WSC, Senior Division, Round 1, Problem 2\nGiven the points \\( F_1 = \\left( -3, 1 - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\right) \\) and \\( F_2 = \\left( -3, 1 + \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\right) \\), we need to determine the set of points \\( P \\) such that \\( |PF_1 - PF_2| = 1 \\). This description suggests that \\( P \\) lies on a hyperbola with foci at \\( F_1 \\) and \\( F_2 \\).\n\nThe distance between the foci is:\n\\[\n|F_1F_2| = \\left| \\left( -3, 1 + \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\right) - \\left( -3, 1 - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} \\right) \\right| = \\left| \\left( 0, \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\right) \\right| = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.\n\\]\n\nFor a hyperbola, the difference in distances to the foci is constant and equal to \\( 2a \\). Given \\( |PF_1 - PF_2| = 1 \\), it follows that \\( 2a = 1 \\) and thus \\( a = \\frac{1}{2} \\).\n\nThe center of the hyperbola \\( C(h, k) \\) is the midpoint of the segment joining the foci:\n\\[\n\\left( h, k \\right) = \\left( \\frac{-3 + (-3)}{2}, \\frac{1 - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + 1 + \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}}{2} \\right) = \\left( -3, 1 \\right).\n\\]\n\nSince \\( F_1 \\) is lower than \\( F_2 \\) and the hyperbola is symmetric with respect to the line \\( y = 1 \\), \\( k = 1 \\).\n\nNext, we need to determine \\( b \\). Using the relationship \\( c^2 = a^2 + b^2 \\) where \\( c = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\) (the distance from the center to each focus), we have:\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2} \\right)^2 = \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right)^2 + b^2 \\implies \\frac{5}{4} = \\frac{1}{4} + b^2 \\implies b^2 = \\frac{5}{4} - \\frac{1}{4} = 1 \\implies b = 1.\n\\]\n\nThus, the equation of the hyperbola is:\n\\[\n\\frac{(y - 1)^2}{\\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right)^2} - \\frac{(x + 3)^2}{1^2} = 1 \\implies \\frac{(y - 1)^2}{\\frac{1}{4}} - \\frac{(x + 3)^2}{1^2} = 1 \\implies 4(y - 1)^2 - (x + 3)^2 = 1.\n\\]\n\nFinally, we find \\( h + k + a + b \\):\n\\[\nh + k + a + b = -3 + 1 + \\frac{1}{2} + 1 = -3 + 1 + \\frac{1}{2} + 1 = -1 + \\frac{1}{2} = -\\frac{2}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} = -\\frac{1}{2}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{1}{2}}.\n\\]",
